A. have manually appended custom contigs in the ref.fa. easiest is to find the ORF in yeastgenome.org and download +/- 1kb flanking seq but that will extend into other ORFs. So find the intergenic region in SGD, add partialORF features in Snapgene or other gene viewers and then copy that.
B. Manually appended gene to GFF file
- would be nice to make this more reproducible
1 nmask_fasta.py # you need to know the start and end of the ORF and chromosome no. of the gene you want to mask
2 fastqc.sh
3 evoVariants.sh
4 Annotate:
A. annotateVCF.sh - using bcftools. was not working very well with lofreq vcf files
